IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- coa30-regulative.l4: the duties, permissions and deadlines of Schedules 10 to 13 written as regulative rules
-- (PARTY ... MUST / MAY ... WITHIN ... HENCE ... LEST ...), lines 20017-20779 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (coa30's ranges).
-- Each rule here has a decision-function twin in the layer-1 module named in its comment, asserted in that module's
-- tests: a DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT on the stable binary, so the traces in
-- coa30-tests-regulative.l4 are read by eye and their results are recorded in NOTES.md (check.sh counts no assertion for them).
--
-- THE CLOCK. A WITHIN counts in whatever unit a file chooses. Here the unit is the one the text uses for that rule, and
-- each rule says which in a comment: months for the three-month period of para 3(5) (a trace event at 2 is inside the
-- period, at 4 is after it) and for "at least once in every calendar year" (the year starts at 0 and ends at 12).
-- Where the text states no time limit (most of these duties) the rule has none: no deadline is invented.
--
-- PARTIES AND ACTS. The core's `Party` lacks the supervisory body, the member of the body, the registered third country
-- auditor and the delegated body, and a part cannot extend the core, so these rules use a party type and an act type of
-- their own (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md for the lead to hoist). Every act is nullary: on the stable binary an input named in
-- an action would match any payload (dialects.md), and nothing here needs a payload.

§ `Schedules 10 to 13 -- the duties as regulative rules`

DECLARE `sch 10 para 2(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
    `sch 10 para 2(4) the recognised supervisory body`
    `sch 10 para 2(4) a person within paragraph 3(6)`
    `sch 10 para 2(4) the registered third country auditor`
    `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order`
    `sch 10 para 2(4) the person who wishes to cite an instrument`

DECLARE `sch 10 para 2(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 para 2(4) give the applicant a written notice of the refusal`
    `sch 10 para 3(3)(a) give written notice of the intention to revoke to the recognised body`
    `sch 10 para 3(3)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the notice to the attention of the members`
    `sch 10 para 3(3)(c) publish the notice`
    `sch 10 para 3(5) make written or oral representations`
    `sch 10 para 3(11)(a) give written notice of the making of the order to the body`
    `sch 10 para 3(11)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the making of the order to the attention of the members`
    `sch 10 para 3(11)(c) publish a notice of the making of the order`
    `sch 10 para 13(12) deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections`
    `sch 10 para 20ZA pay the costs incurred by the competent authority or another recognised supervisory body`
    `sch 12 para 4 pay the costs of maintaining the relevant arrangements`
    `sch 13 para 8(1) print the instrument and make it available to the public`
    `sch 13 para 9(3) cause a copy of the instrument to be endorsed with a certificate`
    `sch 13 para 10(1) make a report to the Secretary of State`
    `sch 13 para 10(3) lay copies of the report before Parliament`

-- ---- Schedule 10 Part 1 ----

-- src:20045 | (4) Where the Secretary of State refuses an application for a recognition order he must give the applicant a written notice to that effect—
-- src:20046 | (a) specifying which requirements, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, are not satisfied, or
-- src:20047 | (b) stating that the application is refused on the ground mentioned in sub-paragraph (3).
@ref sch 10 para 2(4) Where the Secretary of State refuses an application he must give the applicant a written notice (no time limit is stated) (src:20045-20047)
`sch 10 para 2(4) the notice of refusal` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
    MUST `sch 10 para 2(4) give the applicant a written notice of the refusal`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the Secretary of State did not give the applicant a written notice of the refusal (sch 10 para 2(4))"

-- src:20058 | (3) Before revoking a recognition order the Secretary of State must—
-- src:20059 | (a) give written notice of his intention to do so to the recognised body,
-- src:20060 | (b) take such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the notice to the attention of the members of the body, and
-- src:20061 | (c) publish the notice in such manner as he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are in his opinion likely to be affected.
@ref sch 10 para 3(3) Before revoking the Secretary of State must give written notice, take steps and publish the notice (no time limit is stated; twin: sch 10 para 3(3) the Secretary of State has done what he must do before revoking) (src:20058-20061)
`sch 10 para 3(3) the duties before revoking` MEANS
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(3)(a) give written notice of the intention to revoke to the recognised body`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no written notice of the intention to revoke was given to the recognised body (sch 10 para 3(3)(a))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(3)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the notice to the attention of the members`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no steps were taken to bring the notice to the attention of the members (sch 10 para 3(3)(b))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(3)(c) publish the notice`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the notice was not published (sch 10 para 3(3)(c))")

-- src:20065 | (5) A person within sub-paragraph (6) may, within the period of three months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under sub-paragraph (3) or such longer period as the Secretary of State may allow, make written representations to the Secretary of State and, if desired, oral representations to a person appointed for that purpose by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 10 para 3(5) A person within sub-paragraph (6) may make representations within three months beginning with the date of service or publication (clock in months from that date; twin: sch 10 para 3(5) the person may make written and oral representations) (src:20065-20065)
`sch 10 para 3(5) the permission to make representations` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) a person within paragraph 3(6)`
    MAY `sch 10 para 3(5) make written or oral representations`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:20078 | (11) On making an order revoking a recognition order in respect of a body the Secretary of State must—
-- src:20079 | (a) give written notice of the making of the order to the body,
-- src:20080 | (b) take such steps as he considers reasonably practicable for bringing the making of the order to the attention of the members of the body, and
-- src:20081 | (c) publish a notice of the making of the order in such manner as he thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are in his opinion likely to be affected.
@ref sch 10 para 3(11) On making a revocation order the Secretary of State must give written notice, take steps and publish a notice (no time limit is stated) (src:20078-20081)
`sch 10 para 3(11) the duties on making the order` MEANS
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(11)(a) give written notice of the making of the order to the body`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no written notice of the making of the order was given to the body (sch 10 para 3(11)(a))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(11)(b) take reasonably practicable steps to bring the making of the order to the attention of the members`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no steps were taken to bring the making of the order to the attention of the members (sch 10 para 3(11)(b))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
         MUST `sch 10 para 3(11)(c) publish a notice of the making of the order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no notice of the making of the order was published (sch 10 para 3(11)(c))")

-- ---- Schedule 10 Part 2 ----

-- src:20297 | (12) The body must, at least once in every calendar year, deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections conducted under this paragraph.
@ref sch 10 para 13(12) The body must at least once in every calendar year deliver a summary of inspections to the Secretary of State (clock in months from 1 January; twin: sch 10 para 13(12) the body has complied for the calendar year) (src:20297-20297)
`sch 10 para 13(12) the annual summary` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the recognised supervisory body`
    MUST `sch 10 para 13(12) deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections`
    WITHIN 12
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no summary of the results of inspections was delivered to the Secretary of State in the calendar year (sch 10 para 13(12))"

-- src:20350 | 20ZA (1) This paragraph applies where, under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, the competent authority has delegated the task of approving persons as eligible for appointment as statutory auditors to a body (“B”).
-- src:20351 | (2) B must pay the costs incurred by—
-- src:20352 | (a) the competent authority in carrying out activities mentioned in paragraphs 9 to 10C, 12, 13 and 16, or
-- src:20353 | (b) another recognised supervisory body, in carrying out those activities as a result of the competent authority delegating a task to the other body,
-- src:20354 | in relation to any statutory auditor bound by B’s rules.
@ref sch 10 para 20ZA The body must pay the costs incurred by the competent authority or another recognised supervisory body (no time limit is stated; twin: sch 10 para 20ZA the body has paid the costs it must pay) (src:20350-20354)
`sch 10 para 20ZA the duty to pay the costs` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the recognised supervisory body`
    MUST `sch 10 para 20ZA pay the costs incurred by the competent authority or another recognised supervisory body`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the costs incurred by the competent authority or another recognised supervisory body were not paid (sch 10 para 20ZA)"

-- ---- Schedule 12 ----

-- src:20682 | 4 (1) The registered third country auditor must pay any of the costs of maintaining any relevant arrangements which the arrangements provide are to be paid by it.
-- src:20683 | (2) For this purpose “relevant arrangements” are arrangements within paragraph 1 or 2 in which the registered third country auditor is obliged to participate.
@ref sch 12 para 4 The registered third country auditor must pay the costs of maintaining the relevant arrangements that the arrangements provide it is to pay (no time limit is stated; twin: sch 12 para 4 the registered third country auditor has paid the costs it must pay) (src:20682-20683)
`sch 12 para 4 the duty to pay the costs` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the registered third country auditor`
    MUST `sch 12 para 4 pay the costs of maintaining the relevant arrangements`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the costs of maintaining the relevant arrangements were not paid (sch 12 para 4)"

-- ---- Schedule 13 ----

-- src:20738 | 8 (1) Immediately after an instrument is made it must be printed and made available to the public with or without payment.
@ref sch 13 para 8(1) Immediately after an instrument is made it must be printed and made available to the public (WITHIN 0: the same instant; twin: sch 13 para 8(1) the instrument has been printed and made available as required) (src:20738-20738)
`sch 13 para 8(1) the duty to make the instrument available` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order`
    MUST `sch 13 para 8(1) print the instrument and make it available to the public`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the instrument was not printed and made available to the public immediately after it was made (sch 13 para 8(1))"

-- src:20746 | (3) Any person wishing in any legal proceedings to cite an instrument made by the body may require the body to cause a copy of it to be endorsed with such a certificate as is mentioned in this paragraph.
@ref sch 13 para 9(3) On the requirement of a person citing an instrument in legal proceedings the body must cause a copy to be endorsed with a certificate (no time limit is stated) (src:20746-20746)
`sch 13 para 9(3) the duty to endorse a copy` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order`
    MUST `sch 13 para 9(3) cause a copy of the instrument to be endorsed with a certificate`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no copy of the instrument was endorsed with a certificate on the requirement of the person citing it (sch 13 para 9(3))"

-- src:20748 | 10 (1) The body must, at least once in each calendar year for which the delegation order is in force, make a report to the Secretary of State on—
-- src:20749 | (a) the discharge of the functions transferred to it, and
-- src:20750 | (b) such other matters as the Secretary of State may by order require.
@ref sch 13 para 10(1) The body must make a report to the Secretary of State at least once in each calendar year (clock in months from 1 January; twin: sch 13 para 10(1) the body has complied for the calendar year) (src:20748-20750)
`sch 13 para 10(1) the annual report` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the body designated by the delegation order`
    MUST `sch 13 para 10(1) make a report to the Secretary of State`
    WITHIN 12
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no report was made to the Secretary of State in the calendar year (sch 13 para 10(1))"

-- src:20752 | (3) The Secretary of State must lay before Parliament copies of each report received by him under this paragraph.
@ref sch 13 para 10(3) The Secretary of State must lay before Parliament copies of each report received (no time limit is stated; twin: sch 13 para 10(3) the Secretary of State has laid the report before Parliament as required) (src:20752-20752)
`sch 13 para 10(3) the duty to lay the report` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 10 para 2(4) the Secretary of State`
    MUST `sch 13 para 10(3) lay copies of the report before Parliament`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "copies of the report were not laid before Parliament (sch 13 para 10(3))"
